A buff run whose lane ends at a logged hit's ms ends before that hit (engine assumption `boundary-ends`, reading
`before`): the hit is the run's first without it, for the hidden holds' bounds (runBounds) and the log's ends
(heldToLoggedEnds). The c4f3 case it was for: Chen Qianyu's first Wolven Blood final ends at 49958 ms, her crit
attack3's ms; that hit reads with neither the final nor its layers, and its new layer (49958–98995 ms) outlives the
clear. With `listed` (the code) the replay's final ends at 50.00 s, wipes that layer, and her second final comes at
72.30 s against the log's 69.62 s (ending 104.13 s against 99.1 s); with `before` 69.63 → 99.53 s and the third
114.90 → 149.37 s (the log 114.53 → 149.34–150.28 s).

Measured 2026-11-26 (`measure --variant boundary-ends=before`, against 8832cdd): development plain 72.7 → 72.8%, mean
|damage error| 6.3 → 6.4% (10 better, 7 worse, 4 mixed); hold-out plain 82.1 → 82.2%, |error| 7.4% (4 better, 2
worse, 4 mixed); earlier pending 3.5 → 3.4%. c4f3 plain 223 → 233, total −2.9 → −3.2% (per hit 7.79 → 6.63%); 489c
+16, 9090 +10, 0c14 +9; worse 4360 −9 plain (Gilberta's Susceptibility instances: 0.39 → 0.33 at 118–119 s), 9555
−16 (Arcane's doubles Susceptibility ending early at 87–90 s), f879 −5. Excluding an end-boundary where a run of the
same buff and source starts at that ms (a reapplication) didn't change 4360 or 9555 (not measured further).

Dropped: as a rule for every buff it moves as many runs the wrong way; the lane's end at a hit's ms isn't one side of
the hit in general. What would work: the hit's own reading as the evidence (c4f3's 49958 ms hit fits only with the
final off, the check's `boundary` assumption), i.e. a bound only where the end-boundary hit's value decides it.

